<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian aluminium exports up 6.8 pct in Jan/Oct.</title>
<headline>Brazilian aluminium exports up 6.8 pct in Jan/Oct.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian aluminium exports in the first ten months of this year rose 6.8 percent to 708,500 tonnes from 663,700 tonnes in the same period last year, according to the Brazilian Aluminium Association (ABAL).</p>
<p>Exports of ingots and alloys increased 7.2 percent to 611,000 tonnes from 570,100 tonnes in January to October 1995.</p>
<p>Exports of semis and manfactured products also rose 4.2 percent to 97,500 tonnes from 93,600 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Despite the 6.8 percent rise in the quantity of exports, revenue fell 6.7 percent, ABAL said.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
